.TH PATH_DIRLEN_B 3
.SH NAME
path_dirlen_b \- find the length of the directory component of a path
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <path.h>
.PP
.BI "size_t path_dirlen_b(const char* " path ", size_t " size ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B path_dirlen_b
scans the provided
.I path
buffer of length
.I size
to calculate the length of the directory component.
.PP
The function searches for the last occurrence of any path separator character (as defined in the system-specific
.BR PATHSEP_S_MIXED )
and returns the offset representing the length of the directory part of the path. This effectively points to the location just before the basename.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of bytes belonging to the directory part of the path. If no path separator is found, or if the path consists only of a basename, it returns 0.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR path_dirname_b (3),
.BR path_basename2 (3)